  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance to the National Copernicus Capacity Support Action Programme for the Philippines (CopPhil)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;To ascertain the long-term sustainability of the national Copernicus programme for the Philippines (CopPhil) elements for skills development need to be implemented. The proposed TA contract will support exchange of experts from the Philippines to Europe and vice versa. It will facilitate the transfer of knowledge for specific applications as required for the achievement of the overall CopPhil programme objectives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The long-term impact of the CopPhil will be achieved by exposing researchers and graduate students from the Philippines to novel academic programs in Europe specifically designed to strengthen the uptake and evolution of Copernicus data and information. A gender-balanced approach will be adopted to ensure equal access to PH-EU / EU-PH expertise exchange opportunities and equal access to PhD scholarships and MSc ERASMUS+ scholarships opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The TA will secure the achievement of the following results:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- The awareness about benefits and limitations of Earth Observation-derived information is improved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Earth Observation and Geoinformation skills and knowledge are strengthened through exchange of experts and relevant academic programs such as ERASMUS+ - expert exchanges, PhD/MSc scholarships.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Technical aspects and specialised elements of Communication &amp; Visibility (e.g. websites content, social media material, technical brochures, policy papers, workshops material etc.) developed and updated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Technical content and information material linked to all outputs, workshops and trainings developed and disseminated.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
